@meta
id: 16-14
title: Give it room
chapter: 16
type: lesson
skills: window-resize, split-window, window-nav
par: 150
minutes: 6
vscode: drag the divider between the editors until it looks right
open: order.provider.ts

@brief
A split gives each window half the screen, which is the wrong answer
almost every time. A six-line JSON file does not need twenty rows, and
the sixty-line provider under it does. The `Ctrl-W` family resizes
too, and it takes a count.

`Ctrl-W _` makes the current window as tall as it can be; with a count
in front, `6 Ctrl-W _` makes it exactly six lines. `Ctrl-W |` is the
same for width. `Ctrl-W =` puts everything back to equal. `Ctrl-W +`
and `Ctrl-W -` grow and shrink by a line, or by a count. `:resize 6`
does what `6 Ctrl-W _` does if you prefer to see it written down.

Open `errors.json` above the provider, shrink it to six lines so the
provider gets the rest, and make both changes.

  1. `errors.json`: directly under `ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED`, add

         "ORDER_NOT_PENDING": { "statusCode": 409, "sentry": false },

  2. `order.provider.ts`: `ship` throws `ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED` when
     the status is not pending, which is the wrong code. Make it throw
     `ORDER_NOT_PENDING`. The `cancel` method's throw is correct and
     stays.

@keys
| `Ctrl-W _` | this window as tall as possible |
| `6 Ctrl-W _` | this window exactly six lines tall |
| `Ctrl-W \|` | this window as wide as possible; takes a count the same way |
| `Ctrl-W =` | all windows equal again |
| `Ctrl-W +` `Ctrl-W -` | one line taller, one line shorter; take a count |
| `:resize 6` | the command form |

@hints
`:sp errors.json` puts the errors file on top with the cursor in it.
`6 Ctrl-W _` while you are there.
--
`/SHIPPED`, `o`, the new entry, `Esc`. Then `Ctrl-W j` down to the
provider, which now has most of the screen.
--
`/ALREADY_SHIPPED` finds the wrong throw first because `ship` comes
before `cancel`. `cw` from there replaces `ALREADY_SHIPPED` and leaves
`ORDER_` alone; type `NOT_PENDING`. `:wqa`.

@solution
    :sp errors.json<Enter>  6 Ctrl-W _
    /SHIPPED<Enter>  o "ORDER_NOT_PENDING": { "statusCode": 409, "sentry": false }, <Esc>
    Ctrl-W j  /ALREADY_SHIPPED<Enter>  cw NOT_PENDING <Esc>  :wqa<Enter>

Around a hundred and thirty keystrokes. The resize is three of them,
and it is the difference between seeing eight lines of the provider
and seeing forty.

Sizing is not graded and cannot be, but it is the difference between a
layout you keep and one you tear down out of irritation. The pattern
that sticks: open the reference, give it the few lines it needs, work
in the big window, `Ctrl-W =` or `Ctrl-W o` when you are done. Mouse
users drag dividers for the same result and take longer to get there;
`mouse=a` lets you do that in vim too, if you want to feel the
difference.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async findByCustomer(customerId: string) {
    return this.orderRepository.findByCustomer({ customerId });
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'SHIPPED' },
    });
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async findByCustomer(customerId: string) {
    return this.orderRepository.findByCustomer({ customerId });
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_PENDING');
    }

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'SHIPPED' },
    });
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@start errors.json
{
  "ORDER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 404, "sentry": false },
  "ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED": { "statusCode": 409, "sentry": false },
  "CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 404, "sentry": false },
  "REFUND_FAILED": { "statusCode": 502, "sentry": true }
}

@expected errors.json
{
  "ORDER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 404, "sentry": false },
  "ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED": { "statusCode": 409, "sentry": false },
  "ORDER_NOT_PENDING": { "statusCode": 409, "sentry": false },
  "CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 404, "sentry": false },
  "REFUND_FAILED": { "statusCode": 502, "sentry": true }
}
